          "@id": "pkg:apk/dhi/gradle-9@9.8.0-r1?distro=dhi-3.23"
        }
      ],
      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update gradle-9 to 9.8.1-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "GHSA-j5m7-59rp-24f5: during dependency resolution, Gradle does not treat SSL connection failures such as SSLHandshakeException as fatal, so instead of disabling the failing repository it moves on and can resolve the dependency from a later repository an attacker controls. Gradle 9.0.0 to 9.8.0 is affected; 9.8.1 fixes it (https://github.com/gradle/gradle/security/advisories/GHSA-j5m7-59rp-24f5). We read every gradle-9 package published for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository as of 2026-11-27: 22 versions, 9.4.0-r0 to 9.9.2-r0. Each aarch64 package has the same index checksum as the x86_64 package of that version (9.6.1-r3 and 9.6.1-r4 are published for x86_64 only), so we read the x86_64 packages, checked each against its index checksum, and read every jar in them, including nested jars. Each build ships the Gradle release of its package version: the gradle-core, gradle-dependency-management, gradle-resources-http and gradle-launcher jars are named for it, 9.4.0 in 9.4.0-r0 and 9.4.0-r1 and so on up to 9.8.0 in 9.8.0-r1, 9.8.1 in 9.8.1-r0, 9.8.2 in 9.8.2-r0 and 9.8.2-r1, then 9.9.0 to 9.9.2, and their manifests give the same version, with a -SNAPSHOT suffix from 9.8.0-r1 on. Every build before 9.8.1-r0 ships Gradle 9.8.0 or earlier, so the range ends at 9.8.1-r0, the first build with Gradle 9.8.1."
    },
